<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Did the Kings Extend Keegan Murray?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Murray is paid <strong>$24.14m</strong> because Sacramento extended him off his rookie contract before he could reach free agency.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went fourth in 2022 and his rookie contract was worth <strong>$36.37m</strong>.</li>
<li>The club exercised both options on it, in October 2023 and October 2024.</li>
<li>The extension is <strong>$140m</strong> over five years, fully guaranteed.</li>
<li>His salary more than doubled between last season and this one.</li>
<li>There is no option year, so neither side can end it early.</li>
</ul>
<p>He and <a href="/players/deandre-hunter/">De’Andre Hunter</a> were both fourth picks, three drafts apart.</p>

