<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/keegan-murray/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/keegan-murray/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Keegan Murray’s 2026-27 Salary?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Murray earns $24.14m in 2026-27, fourth at Sacramento and the first year of a five-year extension. It rises from $11.14m last season. His career earnings come to $60.51m across five seasons, all at Sacramento. The salary is 12.45% of the club’s $193.95m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Keegan Murray Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Four more guaranteed seasons follow this one, running to 2030-31. He reaches free agency in 2031 at 30, with no option year in between."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Keegan Murray Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $24.14m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Keegan Murray’s Contract With the Kings?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Murray signed a five-year extension worth $140m with Sacramento in 2025, all of it guaranteed. It starts this season. There is no option year in it, so it runs the full five seasons. He reaches free agency in 2031 at 30."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is Keegan Murray Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Murray’s net worth is estimated at around $24.2m, taken from his $60.51m in career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for him. He played two seasons at Iowa and Sacramento took him fourth in 2022, two months before he turned 22."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Did the Kings Extend Keegan Murray?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Murray is paid $24.14m because Sacramento extended him off his rookie contract before he could reach free agency. He and De’Andre Hunter were both fourth picks, three drafts apart."}}]}</script>
